# DITSCF-MS Project Rules

## Before Acting

- This folder is the frontend project only. Do not add backend code or a shared workspace.
- Read `AGENTS.md` before performing project work.
- Inspect relevant project documentation before making assumptions.
- Treat `docs/Project BRS.md` and `docs/Project Vision.md` as primary project references.
- Check existing artifacts before creating new ones.

## Requirements First

- The project is currently technology-agnostic.
- Do not introduce or assume a technology stack unless explicitly approved.
- Separate business requirements from technical decisions.
- Never convert an assumption into a requirement.
- Clearly identify unknowns, conflicts, and decisions that require team discussion.

## System Design

- Design incrementally from requirements toward implementation.
- Prefer conceptual models before technical architecture.
- Keep diagrams and documentation aligned with approved requirements.
- When generating or modifying an artifact, explain what it represents and what assumptions it depends on.

## MCP

- Use MCP tools when they provide an appropriate capability for the task.
- Do not invoke MCP tools merely because they are available.
- Inspect available MCP capabilities before assuming what a tool can do.
- Treat MCP-generated output as a draft until reviewed and approved.
- Never fabricate MCP tool results or claim an action was performed when it was not.
- Record important MCP workflows and decisions under `docs/mcp/`.

## Changes

- Make the smallest appropriate change.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Preserve existing project decisions and business rules.
- Verify changes after completing a task.
